'''''Thoracopterus''''' is an [[extinct]] [[genus]] of overwater gliding [[ray-finned fish]] from the [[Carnian]] age of the [[Late Triassic]]. The [[type species]] is ''T. niederristi''. In 2026, a second species, ''T. polzbergensis'', was erected.<ref name=Italo2022>{{Cite journal |last1=Shen |first1=Chenchen |last2=Arratia |first2=Gloria |date=2021-10-02 |title=Re-description of the sexually dimorphic peltopleuriform fish ''Wushaichthys exquisitus'' (Middle Triassic, China): taxonomic implications and phylogenetic relationships |url=https://doi.org/10.1080/14772019.2022.2029595 |journal=Journal of Systematic Palaeontology |volume=19 |issue=19 |pages=1317–1342 |doi=10.1080/14772019.2022.2029595 |s2cid=247731689 |issn=1477-2019 |url-access=subscription}}</ref><ref>{{Cite book|last1=Tintori |first1=A. |last2=Conedera |first2=D. |last3=Lukeneder |first3=A. |chapter=New Insights into the Fish Assemblage from the Early Carnian of Polzberg in Austria |editor=A. Lukeneder |title=Late Triassic Konservat-Lagerstätten within the Carnian Pluvial Episode. 150 Years of Scientific Excavations in Austria |year=2026 |series=Topics in Geobiology |volume=55 |pages=171–201 |doi=10.1007/978-3-032-19777-1_10 |isbn=9783032197764 |doi-access=free}}</ref>

''Thoracopterus'' had elongate [[pectoral fins]], similar to modern [[Exocoetidae]], which are used to glide overwater in order to escape aquatic [[predators]]. ''Thoracopterus'' represents one of the earliest known example for overwater gliding in [[actinopterygians]].

== Former species==
* {{extinct}}''Thoracopterus martinisi'' <small>Tintori & Sassi, 1992</small> → {{extinct}}''[[Italopterus|Italopterus martinisi]]'' (<small>Tintori & Sassi, 1992</small>)<ref name=Italo2022/>
* {{extinct}}''Thoracopterus magnificus'' <small>Tintori & Sassi, 1992</small> → {{extinct}}''[[Italopterus|Italopterus magnificus]]'' (<small>Tintori & Sassi, 1992</small>)<ref name=Italo2022/>

